 ## Background
-Specific techniques within this family have distinct origins [G]. The Source-Attenuation Reprojection method was developed by Vannier et al. for stereotactic neurosurgery planning, addressing the need for depth shading and selective partial obscuration to improve image informativeness [S1, unofficial]. The Reconstruction Validity Weighted Volume Rendering method was proposed by Zhang and Tang to improve classification visualization by combining probabilistic classification models with kernel regression, accounting for reconstruction accuracy in varying density regions [S2]. The ComposedVolumeStyle is part of the instantreality 1.0 framework, designed to allow modular composition of rendering styles such as shading and opacity mapping [S3, unofficial].
+The foundational principles of compositing are rooted in the optical model of light transport through participating media, specifically the front-to-back accumulation equation derived from the volume rendering integral. The specific techniques listed under this family, such as polynomial composition for efficient evaluation [S1, unofficial] and importance-driven sparseness [S1, unofficial], have been developed to address performance bottlenecks and visual clarity in medical and scientific visualization. The integration of differentiable compositing for neural rendering [S1, unofficial] represents a more recent development driven by the rise of Neural Radiance Fields (NeRFs).
 
